T09 parent integration proposal (apply only in the parent integration checkout)

Three root-level files are touched because T09's registered narrow entry must
discover its test and because crates/wasm-bridge needed a manifest to compile at
all. T09 applied items 1 and 2 locally in the worktree (T21 precedent,
"integration_files_locally_applied") so `pnpm test:task T09` could run and pass;
item 3 was produced mechanically by cargo, never hand-edited.

1. vitest.config.ts — the `web` project must discover T09's lifecycle suite at
   its card-mandated path apps/web/src/lib/editor/t09_lifecycle.test.ts. The
   base include glob covered apps/web/src/features only and matched zero test
   files for the registered command. Exact change (one line):

       { test: { name: 'web', include: ['apps/web/src/features/**/*.test.tsx', 'apps/web/src/lib/**/*.test.ts'], environment: 'jsdom' } },

   Keep passWithNoTests false and every other project boundary unchanged.

2. crates/wasm-bridge/Cargo.toml — the crate had no dependencies while the task
   requires the C3 facade over editor-core/renderer-wgpu/annotation-domain/
   geometry plus serde and uuid (request ids). Declared pins mirror the pins
   already frozen in the workspace (=1.0.229 serde, =0.2.128 wasm-bindgen,
   =0.4.78 wasm-bindgen-futures, =0.6.5 serde-wasm-bindgen, =0.3.105 web-sys,
   =1.18.1 uuid, =1.0.147 serde_json dev). The wasm32-only uuid "js" feature is
   the documented randomness source that makes editor-core's uuid compile for
   wasm32-unknown-unknown (cargo error E0463/"specify a source of randomness"
   otherwise).

3. Cargo.lock — regenerated by cargo when item 2 landed (wasm-bridge dependency
   edges + the uuid/js feature selection). Reproduce with:

       cargo build --target wasm32-unknown-unknown -p wasm-bridge --locked

   Verify with:  cargo test -p wasm-bridge -p editor-core --locked
                 cargo fmt --all -- --check

4. No router/navigation/unified-script/manifest (root package.json,
   pnpm-workspace.yaml, pnpm-lock.yaml, playwright.config.ts, TASKS.json,
   STATUS.json) file is changed by T09. apps/web keeps its existing package.json
   (React 19 + testing-library were already declared by T08; no new JS
   dependency is added anywhere).

5. Optional follow-up for the main agent (NOT applied here): architecture.md
   names packages/wasm-editor as the home of the generated WASM package and
   facade types. The e2e harness builds crates/wasm-bridge via wasm-bindgen into
   target/weblabel-wasm-bridge and apps/web/src/lib/editor/loader.ts loads it
   from /wasm/wasm_bridge.js (DEFAULT_WASM_BRIDGE_URL). When packages/wasm-editor
   is generated (scripts/build-wgpu-probe.mjs style invocation), the loader
   source can point there without code changes.

6. Narrow acceptance after integration (exactly the TASKS.json entry):

       pnpm test:task T09

   Real-browser canvas gate (needs a real WebGPU adapter; this machine has an
   RTX 5060 Ti per reports/T05/gpu-adapter-recheck.md):

       pnpm exec playwright test tests/e2e/t09_canvas.spec.ts --reporter=list

   The spec builds its own wasm bundle (cargo + wasm-bindgen, pinned toolchain)
   and needs no playwright.config.ts change: it launches full Chromium through
   file-level test.use({ channel: 'chromium' }) because the default Playwright
   headless shell has no WebGPU.
